WEBVTT

1
00:00:07.067 --> 00:00:12.007
Vinnie and Mandy quickly followed Varius through the city.

2
00:00:12.008 --> 00:00:16.008
The children were looking at everything around them.

3
00:00:16.009 --> 00:00:20.202
"You are not familiar with our city," Varius said.

4
00:00:20.203 --> 00:00:23.012
The children looked at each other.

5
00:00:23.013 --> 00:00:26.827
"We are new here," Mandy said.

6
00:00:26.828 --> 00:00:30.010
Varius nodded. "I understand.

7
00:00:30.011 --> 00:00:33.017
You will get to know the city very soon."

8
00:00:33.018 --> 00:00:38.079
They passed a few buildings as they walked down a narrow street.

9
00:00:38.080 --> 00:00:42.535
"This is where all the doctors live," Varius explained.

10
00:00:42.536 --> 00:00:47.005
"All the doctors live together?" asked Vinnie.

11
00:00:47.006 --> 00:00:52.622
"No, they have their own homes," Varius laughed.

12
00:00:52.623 --> 00:00:54.879
"But the city is divided up.

13
00:00:54.880 --> 00:00:57.449
The doctors all live in one area.

14
00:00:57.450 --> 00:00:59.751
The butchers live in another.

15
00:00:59.752 --> 00:01:02.467
It's easier to find people."

16
00:01:02.468 --> 00:01:07.277
A few minutes later, they arrived in the butchers' area.

17
00:01:07.278 --> 00:01:11.556
People lived in apartments on top of their shops.

18
00:01:11.557 --> 00:01:15.553
Children were outside playing some kind of game.

19
00:01:15.554 --> 00:01:18.654
They had drawn squares in the dirt.

20
00:01:18.655 --> 00:01:22.201
Each square had a rock or a shell.

21
00:01:22.202 --> 00:01:26.555
"It looks like tic-tac-toe!" said Vinnie.

22
00:01:26.556 --> 00:01:28.714
"Sorry to interrupt your game,"

23
00:01:28.715 --> 00:01:32.356
said Varius, leaning over the children.

24
00:01:32.357 --> 00:01:35.219
"Do you know where Melus the stable boy lives?"

25
00:01:35.220 --> 00:01:36.862
"He is over there.

26
00:01:36.863 --> 00:01:40.356
His mother is sick," a girl said.

27
00:01:40.357 --> 00:01:42.941
She pointed to a house.

28
00:01:42.942 --> 00:01:48.217
Varius and the children walked over and knocked on the door.

29
00:01:48.218 --> 00:01:50.426
Melus answered.

30
00:01:50.427 --> 00:01:56.259
"We know about your mother, but your master Aquila is in danger," Varius said.

31
00:01:56.260 --> 00:01:59.541
He explained about Brutus.

32
00:01:59.542 --> 00:02:04.874
"My mother is feeling better, praise the gods," Melus said.

33
00:02:04.875 --> 00:02:09.341
"My father is with her now, so I can return to the stables.

34
00:02:09.342 --> 00:02:12.074
What should I do about Brutus?"

35
00:02:12.075 --> 00:02:20.207
"Don't let anyone near Aquila's horses," said Mandy, "or they will be poisoned."

36
00:02:20.208 --> 00:02:25.012
"I will guard my master's horses with my life!" Melus cried.

37
00:02:25.013 --> 00:02:27.339
He ran out the door.

38
00:02:27.340 --> 00:02:31.479
Varius and the children left Melus' house.

39
00:02:31.480 --> 00:02:36.436
"Do you trust Melus?" Mandy asked.

40
00:02:36.437 --> 00:02:41.209
"Yes, I do. Melus was chosen to look after Aquila's horses.

41
00:02:41.210 --> 00:02:45.673
That is a very special job," explained Varius.

42
00:02:45.674 --> 00:02:47.451
"Melus knows this.

43
00:02:47.452 --> 00:02:50.681
So he will not betray his master."

44
00:02:50.682 --> 00:02:54.942
"What should we do now?" asked Vinnie.

45
00:02:54.943 --> 00:02:59.311
"We must speak with Master Antonius," said Varius.

46
00:02:59.312 --> 00:03:03.289
"He is responsible for our festivals and public buildings.

47
00:03:03.290 --> 00:03:07.658
As Septimus said, he is in charge of today's race."

48
00:03:07.659 --> 00:03:12.140
"When does the race begin?" asked Mandy.

49
00:03:12.141 --> 00:03:15.206
Varius looked up at the sun.

50
00:03:15.207 --> 00:03:16.825
"It will begin soon.

51
00:03:16.826 --> 00:03:19.741
We must hurry," he said.

52
00:03:19.742 --> 00:03:25.154
Varius stopped in front of a large house with a stone fountain.

53
00:03:25.155 --> 00:03:29.621
"Master Antonius lives here," said Varius.

54
00:03:29.622 --> 00:03:38.883
A man with a hammer was bent close to the ground.
